section.animate-in.space-y-3
	a.text-sm.nav-link.inline-flex.items-center.gap-1(href="/examples/tron") ← TRON examples
	h1.text-4xl.font-bold.tracking-tight.leading-none
		GradientText Remote pickers
	p.max-w-prose.leading-relaxed(class="text-fg-muted")
		| Autocomplete and MultiSelect take a
		code source
		| instead of
		code items
		| : a debounced function of the typed text that resolves the options. Here it is
		code GET /api/notes/search?q=
		| , capped at 20 rows, so the picker works the same over ten notes or ten million.

section.animate-in-delayed.pt-8
	.grid.gap-6(class="md:grid-cols-2")
		Card
			+snippet('header')
				h3.text-base.font-semibold Autocomplete
			Field(label="Note" name="note" help="Type to search titles")
				Autocomplete(source!="{searchNotes}" bind:value!="{one}" placeholder="Search notes…")
			p.text-sm.mt-3(class="text-fg-muted")
				| Selected id:
				code {one ?? '—'}
		Card
			+snippet('header')
				h3.text-base.font-semibold MultiSelect
			Field(label="Notes" name="notes" help="Labels of picked options survive new searches")
				MultiSelect(source!="{searchNotes}" bind:value!="{many}" placeholder="Pick several…" minChars!="{0}")
			p.text-sm.mt-3(class="text-fg-muted")
				| Selected ids:
				code {many.length ? many.join(', ') : '—'}

section.pt-10.space-y-2
	h2.text-lg.font-semibold What to look at
	ul.list-disc.pl-5.space-y-1.text-sm(class="text-fg-muted")
		li
			| Requests fire 200 ms after the last keystroke (
			code debounce
			| ), and a slow earlier response never overwrites a newer one.
		li
			| The search route reuses
			code listQuery()
			| for
			code q
			| and
			code pageSize
			| ; responses under 1 KB are plain JSON even with the TRON Accept header.
		li
			| Swap
			code source
			| for
			code items
			| and both components fall back to client-side filtering — same markup, same keyboard handling.

<script>
	import { searchNotes } from '$lib/norns/notes/client/api'

	one .= $state undefined
	many .= $state []
</script>
